/* What goes into the NREMT flashcard deck (nremt/assets/flashcards.json),
   read by scripts/build-nremt-flashcards.mjs.

   Four sources, and only the last is typed out here:
     1. glossary   every term in nremt/data/glossary.json (the glossary page's source).
                   GLOSSARY_DOMAIN files each term under one of the six
                   NREMT domains; a term the glossary gains without being filed
                   here fails the build, so nothing slips in unsorted.
     2. mnemonic   every card on nremt/mnemonics.html, read out of the page.
     3. reference  the rows of the tables on nremt/reference-cards.html named
                   in REFERENCE_TABLES (found by header row, like the ochem
                   deck's rules).
     4. fact       FACTS below: the numbers and rules the exam keeps asking
                   for, one per card, each tied to the study-notes section
                   that teaches it (the build checks the section exists).

   CLINICAL CONTENT. Written to the EMT scope of practice and the 2025 AHA
   guidelines, and kept consistent with nremt/assets/study-notes.json — where
   the notes give a number, the card gives the same one. Doses are the ones
   commonly taught; the card says so, and local protocol governs. A fact card
   is plain text (the build escapes it), one idea per card, short enough to
   answer before flipping.

   Card ids are permanent (progress is stored against them): a fact's id is
   its `id` field, never derived from its wording, so rewording a card keeps
   its schedule. Retire an id rather than reuse it. */

